      "claim": "Net surplus as a function of quantity Q is S(Q)=TB(Q)−TC(Q), so dS/dQ = MB(Q)−MC(Q).",
      "evidence": "Definition of marginal benefit (dTB/dQ) and marginal cost (dTC/dQ).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The interior maximum of S(Q) occurs where its derivative is zero, i.e., MB(Q)=MC(Q).",
      "evidence": "Calculus first‑order condition for a maximum: set dS/dQ = 0.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Thus the consumer will stop eating when the marginal benefit of the next cookie equals its marginal cost; any further cookie would reduce net surplus.",
      "evidence": "If MB>MC, adding a unit raises S; if MB<MC, adding a unit lowers S. Equality is the indifference point.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [3]
    },
    {
